  {
    "sha": "3718134253c1182e341fc6f483a7c2b2759a42e6",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDM3MTgxMzQyNTNjMTE4MmUzNDFmYzZmNDgzYTdjMmIyNzU5YTQyZTY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-19T01:27:08Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-19T01:27:08Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(import): hold a STEP face's facets to its surface\n\nA cylinder face with a hole in it (a bar with a cross hole) imported\nwith wall facets that ran through the solid, up to 25 mm inside the\ntrue cylinder: the kernel's parameter grid has no point inside such a\nface, and its triangulation joined each rim edge to the hole's rim a\nquarter turn away. The importer reported the tolerance it asked for.\nEvery gouge law then judged cuts against a part that was too small, so\na tilted slot 0.5 mm into the bar came out clean and posted (#2600).\n\nThe importer now measures each curved elementary face's inside facet\nedges against the surface, splits an edge that stands more than two\npass tolerances off it, and reports a chord height it cannot refine\naway as the import's chord error (reduced fidelity, #864). Boundary\nedges are never split, so the shell stays closed.\n\nPinned by tilted_gouge: a_tilted_slot_into_the_step_bar_is_refused,\nthe_step_bars_wall_facets_lie_on_the_cylinder.\n\nFixes #2600\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "f5d6b027fb5ac55a15a1fe7ab8336985160a894a",
